<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2" id="process_reextractspikes_stderiv">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>process_reextractspikes_stderiv</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>process_reextractspikes_stderiv</refname>
		<refpurpose>second-pass spike detection on a spatial+temporal derivative signal with timestamp masking.</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsynopsisdiv>
		<cmdsynopsis>
			<command>process_reextractspikes_stderiv</command>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-n</option> <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-c</option> <replaceable>channels</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-w</option> <replaceable>waveformLength</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-p</option> <replaceable>peakSample</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-l</option> <replaceable>peakSearchLength</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-r</option> <replaceable>refractoryPeriod</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-f</option> <replaceable>thresholdFactor</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-B</option> <replaceable>startByte</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><option>-Z</option> <replaceable>sizeBytes</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-T</option> <replaceable>sdiff|stderiv</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-d</option> <replaceable>sdiffOrder</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-P</option> <replaceable>sdiffPairs</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-S</option> <replaceable>auto|prev|zero</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-m</option> <replaceable>maskBase</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-M</option> <replaceable>maskHalfWidth</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-i</option> <replaceable>inputFile</replaceable></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-v</option></arg>
			<arg choice="opt"><option>-h</option></arg>
			<arg choice="plain"><replaceable>basename</replaceable></arg>
		</cmdsynopsis>
	</refsynopsisdiv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>DESCRIPTION</title>
		<para>
			Spatial-derivative + temporal first-difference variant of
			<command>process_reextractspikes</command>.  Thresholds are
			computed internally over
			<replaceable>startByte</replaceable>..<replaceable>startByte+sizeBytes</replaceable>
			using the Quiroga (2004) robust noise estimator, exactly as
			<command>process_extractspikes_stderiv</command> computes them:
			<option>-T</option> <literal>sdiff</literal> (default) measures the
			noise on the spatial derivative, <literal>stderiv</literal> on the
			detection signal.  Detection runs
			on the stderiv shadow signal. The program writes
			<filename>basename.res.N</filename> and
			<filename>basename.spkD.N</filename>; the
			<filename>.spkD.N</filename> windows hold the same transformed
			signal (spatial derivative plus temporal first difference) that
			<command>process_extractspikes_stderiv</command> writes, so they
			project through the same <filename>.pcaD.N</filename> basis.
		</para>
		<para>
			<option>-m</option> (mask basename, default
			<replaceable>basename</replaceable>), <option>-M</option> (mask
			half-width in samples, default the refractory period) and
			<option>-i</option> (input file, default
			<filename>basename.fil</filename>) work as in
			<command>process_reextractspikes</command>; <option>-v</option>
			is verbose, <option>-h</option> prints help.
		</para>
		<para>
			<option>-S</option> sets the seed of each written window's temporal
			difference: <literal>prev</literal> (the spatial derivative of the
			sample before the window, as <command>process_extractspikes_stderiv -R</command>
			writes), <literal>zero</literal> (the older extractor), or
			<literal>auto</literal> (default): follow the reference
			<filename>maskBase.spk.N</filename> paired with
			<filename>maskBase.res.N</filename>, using <literal>prev</literal>
			when that cannot be decided.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>SEE ALSO</title>
		<para>
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_reextractspikes</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<command>process_extractspikes_stderiv</command> (no manual page; run it with <option>-h</option>),
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_shadowcluster</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
		</para>
	</refsect1>

</refentry>
